{# The organisation the visitor came for (issue #449): the logo the tenant declared, with its name as the
   text that stands in for the image, so that a reader who does not see it is told who they came for. The
   browser of that reader loads the image, never the provider, and no referrer goes with the request; the
   policy of the page names the origin it is served from and no other, which reading the tenant names
   (TenantExtension, issue #926).

   A tenant that declared no logo renders nothing at all, which is the page every deployment has been
   served so far. The colours it declared are not here: a colour is a look, and the look of these pages is
   the application's (architecture §5.2), which reads them from the same object.

   The provider ships the shape and the words, never a class: "data-tenant" is what a stylesheet reads, and
   an application that wants this somewhere else includes this one file. #}
{% set tenant = beffroi_tenant() %}
{% if tenant is not null and tenant.logoUri is not null %}
    <header data-tenant="brand">
        <img data-tenant="logo" src="{{ tenant.logoUri }}" alt="{{ tenant.name }}" referrerpolicy="no-referrer">
    </header>
{% endif %}
